  "notes": "Cross-dataset binary fault detection (healthy vs faulty). Transfer type: real_to_real (source=DronePropA REAL-PUBLIC, target=TII REAL-PUBLIC). Level: time_broad (feature_dim=54). Direction 1: DronePropA->TII (train=127: 40H/87F, test=99: 19H/80F). Direction 2: TII->DronePropA (train=99, test=127). DronePropA: F0=healthy, F1/F2/F3=faulty (127 flights, REAL experimental QDrone + OptiTrack, Mendeley CC BY 4.0; 130 nominal, 3 missing \u2014 see data/source/dronepropa_exclusion_manifest.json). TII: class 0=healthy, class 1-4=faulty (99 missions, real experimental flights). Features: 6 channels (gyro xyz + accel xyz), sampling-rate invariant. No order-normalized (1P/2P) features: DronePropA 24.41 Hz peak is a control loop rate (1000/41 Hz), not propeller RPM (appears in motor_CMD and ESC telemetry, r=-0.753 vs throttle, pegged across all flights). TII ~40 Hz peak is real propeller RPM but varies 32-48 Hz. CORAL: linear Correlation Alignment (Sun & Saenko 2016). NOTE: The 0.929 DP->TII RandomForest macro_F1 (time_broad) is UNDER RE-AUDIT. The permutation test in diagnostics/uav_cross_dataset_scrutiny.json only shuffles labels against fixed predictions and does NOT retrain under the null, so it is not a valid test of significance. A proper permutation test (retrain per shuffle) and domain-confound checks are pending."
